### ======================================================================
### 9. WHAT THE DATABASE SAW (run in PowerShell, not here)
### ======================================================================
###   docker exec -it appointme-db psql -U appointme -d appointme -c "SELECT id, customer_id, appointment_id, number, status, subtotal, tax_total, total FROM invoices ORDER BY id;"
###   docker exec -it appointme-db psql -U appointme -d appointme -c "SELECT * FROM invoice_counters;"
###
### EXPECT (the year is the current year in Athens):
###    id | customer | appt | number         | status | subtotal | tax   | total
###     1 |        1 |      | INV-2026-0001  | PAID   |    99.99 | 24.00 | 123.99
###     2 |        1 |      |                | VOID   |    10.00 |  0.00 |  10.00
###     3 |        1 |      |                | DRAFT  |     0.00 |  0.00 |   0.00
###     4 |        2 |      | INV-2026-0002  | VOID   |    40.00 |  9.60 |  49.60
###     5 |        1 |      | INV-2026-0003  | ISSUED |    30.00 |  0.00 |  30.00
###     6 |        2 |    1 |                | VOID   |    25.00 |  6.00 |  31.00
###     7 |        2 |    1 |                | DRAFT  |    25.00 |  6.00 |  31.00
###   counters: tenant 1, year 2026, last_number 3
